{
  "id": "Compound::DB01403 - Gene::1133",
  "verbalization": "Methotrimeprazine is likely to interact with Chrm5 through a mechanism involving muscarinic acetylcholine receptors. The evidence suggests that Methotrimeprazine binds to Chrm4, which is involved in the activation of muscarinic acetylcholine receptors. This binding leads to the participation of Chrm4 in G-protein coupled receptor activities, ultimately resulting in the participation of Chrm5 in these processes. The overlapping pathways highlight a potential role for Methotrimeprazine in modulating muscarinic receptor activity, possibly through a G-protein-mediated signaling cascade. The consistent involvement of Chrm5 in multiple receptor activity pathways underscores its role as a downstream target of muscarinic signaling, suggesting that Methotrimeprazine may influence Chrm5 through a complex network of receptor interactions.",
